===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[entrap]]; to catch in a [[snare]] or [[trap]].
#* {{RQ:Thomson Autumn|year=1768|page=160|lines=1289–1292|passage=Let ''theſe'' / '''Inſnare''' the vvretched in the toils of lavv, / Fomenting diſcord, and perplexing right, / An iron race!}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1887|author=w:Æsop|title=Three Hundred Æsop's Fables|translators=George Fyler Townsend
|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Three_Hundred_%C3%86sop%27s_Fables/The_Geese_and_the_Cranes
|passage=The Geese and the Cranes fed in the same meadow. A birdcatcher came to '''ensnare''' them in his nets.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=w:Plato|title=Sophist|translators=Lesley Brown; [[w:Stephanus pagination|250d-e]]
|passage=When we were asked to what one should apply the name “what is not”, we were '''ensnared''' in total paradox. Remember?}}
# To [[entangle]]; to [[enmesh]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=w:Edwin Black
|title=Internal Combustion
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL4103950W
|passage=But electric vehicles and the batteries that made them run became '''ensnared''' in corporate scandals, fraud, and monopolistic corruption that shook the confidence of the nation and inspired automotive upstarts.}}

